.md
## Improved formatting of PlotLegends and FrameLabels
Due to a Unicode decoding issue, it wasn't previously possible to embed LaTeX in plot-axis labels or legends, or to mix it with regular labels.

For example, suppose you want to place a LaTeX equation as a plot legend:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
## Improved formatting of PlotLegends and FrameLabels
Due to a Unicode decoding issue, it wasn't previously possible to embed LaTeX in plot-axis labels or legends, or to mix it with regular labels.

For example, suppose you want to place a LaTeX equation as a plot legend:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Plot[x x, {x,0,1}, PlotLegends->Placed[{
  TeXView["x^2"]
}, {0.2,0.6}]]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(*VB[*)(Legended[ToExpression[FrontEndRef["9a89c92a-8f59-44db-b9c2-3a051a7fc010"], InputForm], Placed[LineLegend[{Directive[Opacity[1.], RGBColor[0.24, 0.6, 0.8], AbsoluteThickness[2]]}, {TeXView[Offload[URLDecode["x%5E2"]]]}, LegendMarkers -> None, LabelStyle -> {}, LegendLayout -> "Column"], {0.2, 0.6}, Identity]])(*,*)(*"1:"*)(*]VB*)

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
Here we used `TeXView` directly with TeX code inside. Sometimes, if the expression is too large, you may set the size and anchor manually to better position your legend item:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Here we used `TeXView` directly with TeX code inside. Sometimes, if the expression is too large, you may set the size and anchor manually to better position your legend item:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Plot[x x, {x,0,1}, PlotLegends->Placed[{
  TeXView["x^2~\\text{function}", ImageSize->{150,30}, AlignmentPoint->{Left,Center}]
}, {0.2,0.6}]]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(*VB[*)(Legended[ToExpression[FrontEndRef["48b501c0-843e-4879-ad8a-d9c307ccc81c"], InputForm], Placed[LineLegend[{Directive[Opacity[1.], RGBColor[0.24, 0.6, 0.8], AbsoluteThickness[2]]}, {TeXView[Offload[URLDecode["x%5E2~%5Ctext%7Bfunction%7D"]], ImageSize -> {150, 30}, AlignmentPoint -> {Left, Center}]}, LegendMarkers -> None, LabelStyle -> {}, LegendLayout -> "Column"], {0.2, 0.6}, Identity]])(*,*)(*"1:"*)(*]VB*)

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
Use `Row` to combine LaTeX expressions with normal text labels.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Display: markdown
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Use `Row` to combine LaTeX expressions with normal text labels.

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Plot[x x, {x,0,1}, PlotLegends->Placed[{
  Row[{
    TeXView["x^2"],
    "function"  
  }]
}, {0.2,0.6}]]

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Type: Output
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
(*VB[*)(Legended[ToExpression[FrontEndRef["523b0a2f-4641-402a-a871-e20a60848509"], InputForm], Placed[LineLegend[{Directive[Opacity[1.], RGBColor[0.24, 0.6, 0.8], AbsoluteThickness[2]]}, {Row[{TeXView[Offload[URLDecode["x%5E2"]]], "function"}]}, LegendMarkers -> None, LabelStyle -> {}, LegendLayout -> "Column"], {0.2, 0.6}, Identity]])(*,*)(*"1:"*)(*]VB*)

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
Props:
  Hidden: true
Type: Input
%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
.md
The same can be done with the `FrameLabel` of your plot; you can put `TeXView`, or, in general, any other expression, alongside normal text:

%-------------------------------------------------------------------------%
